-- scripts/dst/park_wake_dst.ail
--
-- PLAN-002 W4 Part 6 (ADR-002 D2/D3): the park-and-wake fixtures, exactly the
-- ADR's list, plus Part 7's metric. Every run drives the TRACED entry with a
-- scripted (or recording) world whose `wakes` queue holds observations, never
-- worlds (§1 row 8), and an extension that serves `Delegate` with a `wait` and
-- `DelegateCheck` with `settled`, the W1b producer's shapes.
--
-- Fixtures (each prints its own ✓/✗ rows):
--   success (Settled) · Lost · OperatorInput leaving the delegate pending ·
--   two delegates with one wake · HostError leaving the wait open, then a second
--   park succeeding · TimedOut removing only the timer · re-delegation ("both
--   are open") · mid-park abort and restart
-- Controls:
--   wrong handle (the re-issue bound, §8.3/R1/R2) · duplicate or late wake ·
--   missing wake (HostError at the exhaustion point, directly) · stale world ·
--   empty stop with open waits · the DP7-rejected candidate with open waits
-- Plus: two runs from one script (determinism) and the saved-program replay
-- through `recording_wake`; Part 7's metric on each channel separately.
--
-- `TimerWait` HAS NO PRODUCER in this plan (review change 18). The `TimedOut`
-- fixture constructs it directly, as the fixture extension's own `wait`
-- metadata; no production code path emits one.
--
-- What the in-process run cannot see is on stdout, and `run_park_wake.sh` reads
-- it: the dropped-reply `warning` count per frame (R2: nothing is appended), the
-- conversation loop's `session_suspend` for a mid-park `restart`, and the
-- byte-identity of the two determinism frames. Frames are
-- `PARK_RUN_BEGIN <label>` / `PARK_RUN_END <label>`.

module scripts/dst/park_wake_dst

